# CI/CD + README + GitHub Releases

Standing preference: development uses CI/CD end-to-end; keep README current; record each display-version ship on GitHub.

## Do

- **CI:** Live-line PRs/pushes touching `app_25.0/**`, `scripts/**`, or `.github/workflows/**` must run meaningful offline checks (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`: valuation formulas + Phase 1). Do not reintroduce path filters that skip the live app tree (vacuous green).
- **Ship:** `Rscript scripts/deploy_app_21.R` → baseline update → push. Prefer a `CHANGELOG.md` entry for the new `display_version`, then `bash scripts/record_github_release.sh v…` (soft-fail without `gh`/token; never commit secrets).
- **README:** After live-line / process changes, update root README (and `app_25.0/README` history only when needed) so pointers match `app_25.0/` and `DEPLOY_BASELINE.txt`.

## Do not

- Invent CHANGELOG history without git / baseline evidence.
- Deploy solely to demo Release docs from Cloud Agents without credentials / request.
- Put `GH_TOKEN` or shinyapps secrets in git.

See root `CHANGELOG.md`, `README.md` CI/CD section, and Project preference `workflows/ci-cd-readme-releases.md`.
